{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1mStPo6p6yyw1BfBVJE", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I signed off with low confidence (0.4). I found and reported one bug, and the sweep left parts of the three areas untested.\n\n**Bug filed (developer confirmed it):** on the Add note screen, Back closes the screen with no discard prompt after a note type swap.\n- Steps: type \"gato\" in Front, switch the type from Basic to Cloze, press Back.\n- Without the swap, the same Back press shows \"Discard current input?\".\n- This is the Add note dismissal change from the build.\n\n**Checked and fine:**\n- **Filtered deck builder:** the \"Cards selected by\" dropdown listed all 11 criteria. Building a filtered deck on the empty Default deck gave the expected \"No cards matched\" error. Backing out of the builder prompted \"Discard changes?\".\n- **Deck options, New cards/day:** I set the \"This deck\" limit on Spanish to 15. It was still 15 when I reopened the screen, and French still showed 20.\n\n**Not tested:**\n- Saving a new note, and editing an existing note.\n- The Preset and Today only tabs on the daily limits.\n- Rotating the screen.\n- Anything else on the deck options screen.\n\nAlong the way, tapping the icon at the top of the reviewer ended the review (\"Congratulations! You have finished for today.\"). I never identified what that icon does, so I don't know whether that behavior is correct."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 497, "cache_read_input_tokens": 36725, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 497}, "output_tokens": 447, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "547703f